---
import BaseLayout from "../../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import MetaPill from "../../../components/ui/MetaPill.astro";
import registry from "../../../data/phase-81-universal-service-essential-systems-public-option-delivery-registry.json";

const floors = registry.service_floor_universal_access_dossiers;
const affordability = registry.affordability_cross_subsidy_coverage_ledgers;
const providers = registry.provider_plurality_interoperability_continuity_registers;
const restoration = registry.rights_quality_step_in_restoration_ledgers;
---

<BaseLayout title="Universal Service And Essential Systems | FTFN" description="Eight inactive service-floor dossiers and eight each of affordability, provider-continuity, and rights-restoration ledgers.">
  <section class="page-section hero" data-essential-service-registry><div class="hero__copy"><div class="eyebrow">FTFN / Universal Service</div><h1 class="page-title">Infrastructure coverage is not access, and average uptime is not universal quality.</h1><p class="lede">Phase 81 separates essential-service classification, enforceable floors, eligible publics, access, affordability, cross-subsidy, coverage, provider plurality, public options, interoperability, continuity, user rights, quality, provider failure, step-in, rationing, restoration, and remedy.</p><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label="8 inactive floor dossiers" tone="possibility" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive affordability ledgers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive provider registers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive restoration ledgers" /><MetaPill label="0 service decisions" tone="review" /></div></div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Essential Services And Floors</div><h2>Eight universal-service floor dossiers remain closed.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/universal-service-doctrine-001/">Read the universal-service doctrine</a></div><div class="grid">{floors.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.service_floor_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="14 service classes" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/essential-services/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Authority, classification, eligible publics, floors, baselines, access, capacity, funding, standards, rights, continuity, options, review, and receipts remain inactive.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Affordability And Coverage</div><h2>Eight affordability and cross-subsidy ledgers contain no decision.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/affordability-cross-subsidy-001/">Read the affordability method</a></div><div class="grid">{affordability.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.affordability_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="12 coverage dimensions" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/essential-services/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.affordability_cross_subsidy_coverage_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Costs, burdens, protections, funding, subsidies, cross-subsidies, connections, take-up, capacity, quality parity, and triggers remain empty.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Providers, Standards And Continuity</div><h2>Eight provider and continuity registers remain inactive.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/public-options-provider-plurality-001/">Read the provider plurality guide</a></div><div class="source-list">{providers.map((record) => <article class="source-row"><div><h3><a href={'/evidence/essential-services/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.provider_plurality_interoperability_continuity_register_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Provider models, open standards, conformance, portability, maintenance, reserves, mutual aid, exercises, step-in readiness, and orderly exit remain unverified.</p></div><MetaPill label={record.provider_decision} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Rights, Quality And Restoration</div><h2>Eight step-in and restoration ledgers contain no intervention.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/provider-failure-step-in-public-option-001/">Read the step-in method</a></div><div class="grid">{restoration.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><h3><a href={'/evidence/essential-services/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.rights_quality_step_in_restoration_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Rights, complaints, appeals, remedies, quality, reliability, maintenance, provider failure, intervention, rationing, restoration, normalization, and correction remain inactive.</p><MetaPill label={record.restoration_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section briefing-band"><div class="briefing-band__copy"><div class="eyebrow">Public Contract</div><h2>Inspect the empty universal-service state.</h2><p>The export publishes all service-floor, affordability, access, provider, standard, continuity, rights, quality, intervention, and restoration controls. It contains no adopted floor, tariff, subsidy, provider, standard, finding, activation, remedy, receipt, score, rank, or stage change.</p></div><article class="record-card"><a class="inline-link" href="/data/universal-service-essential-systems-public-options.json">Universal service JSON</a></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
